# Kids sites — deploy after owner OK (public paths)

When **public** kids static sites change — Halalit, Crocheter, LoreKeeper, hub — **do not deploy automatically**.

**Owner-only** (Maestro's, envDyst, Climatic Mysteries): follow **`owner-only-auto-deploy`** — verify, then deploy without asking.

When **all** paths in `deploy-kids-sites.sh` change but edits are **only** under `maestrosOdyssey/www/` or `envDyst/www/`, use the owner-only rule (`--site=maestros` or `--site=envdyst` limits restarts). **LoreKeeper-only** edits use `bash top/scripts/deploy-lorekeeper.sh` after owner OK — does not restart Halalit.

Follow **`warn-before-live-user-impact`**: give a **Deploy check** before running the script.

**Public paths** — deploy only when the owner clearly says **deploy**, **deploy now**, **ship it**, or **yes**. Deploy check **first in the same turn**, then run deploy.

**Owner-only paths** — after verify (see **`owner-only-auto-deploy`**), deploy in the **same turn** without waiting for those words. Still give the brief deploy check.

From **repo root** when approved:

```bash
bash top/scripts/deploy-kids-sites.sh
```

**Usually touched paths:** `maestrosOdyssey/www/`, `crocheter/www/`, `envDyst/www/`, `halalit/www/`, `lorekeeper/www/`, `top/directory/www/` (hub), `top/_shared/serve_static_https.py`, `lorekeeper/lorekeeper_api.py`, `top/nginx/oddtrove.art.conf` (LoreKeeper nginx — reload nginx separately after deploy script). LoreKeeper-only deploy: `bash top/scripts/deploy-lorekeeper.sh`.

**Halalit:** Same rule for `halalit/www/`. `halalit/.cursor/private/` design-notes are local-only and never deployed.

If SSH or the script fails, say so clearly and leave the command for a retry.

For edits that **do not** affect those deploy paths, skip deploy.
